A||||9||curtis||please help!!!||||8||
Z||000000||curtis||08-11-2001||08:11 PM||||One day my brothers 88 formula died on the highway at 70mph. We thought maybe fuel problem, it sat for a while because of cash. We recently changed all 6 injectors and fuel regulator. It turns over but will not start. We checked for spark on #5 plug. Can smell fuel. Checked battery grounds. When it first happened I put in a new ignition module to check and it didn't start. We can't figure this one out could it be the ECM? Is there a way to check the ECM. Also now when we try to start it after sitting for a couple of months, it has a sound under the plenum similar to a squeaky belt. <BR>Please help with this one!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||PBJ||08-11-2001||09:00 PM||||Sounds like you will need to find if it has spark or not. If your ses light comes on with the key on, than I would not fail the ecm yet.<P>Did you replace the ignition module with a known good/new one?||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||08-11-2001||09:20 PM||||The ECM does not control spark until the car starts or close to it (400 RPM). If the ECM was bad, it would start and die.<P>Is there spark when you pull a wire and hold it near ground? Is the distributor turning?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||curtis||08-11-2001||09:25 PM||||The ignition module was brand new ac delco that worked fine in my 86gt. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||86seyellow||08-11-2001||09:34 PM||||I had the same problem, thought it was ignition. changed all including distributor, then took it to the shop, It was the fuel pump. It was pumping but low pressure. Changed and it has never ran better ($800 I spent total)<BR><P>------------------<BR>if you saw a yellow streak go by you really fast it was a fiero<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||JR||08-11-2001||10:13 PM||||Yes, most probably require new fuel pump assembly. Had same problem on my 86GT, but only when engine was hot, strangely no problem during the fall and winter but the fuel pump was getting louder (buzzing).  Finally after some 2 years of increasingly noisy fuel pump no more sarty.  Fuel pump cured it.  Incidently this happened twice as the first fuel pump (a Walbro unit) didn't last a year before the symptoms and a buzzing pump failed.  Had it replaced with the OEM, been good for 3years now<P>------------------<BR>85GT (daily driver 120,000 miles)<BR>88GT (highly modified sunday driver)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||08-11-2001||10:30 PM||||I had a similar problem on my Formula.  It turned out to be the ECM wasn't getting power, so the injectors weren't firing.  <P>Check to see if you're getting spark.<BR>Check to see if you're getting about 45psi fuel pressure.<BR>Is the SES light coming on when you turn the key to run (engine off)?  That was my cue that the ECM wasn't getting power.  <BR>Do you hear the fuel pump run when you first turn the key?<P>In my case, I had good fuel pressure, good spark, and good air supply.  But it wouldn't fire because the injectors were firing.  So, no fuel to the engine.  1st diagnostic was a bad fuel pump, until we checked the fuel pressure.<P>Check those items and let us know what you find.  We'll get you running yet!<P>And I'd like to take another moment to thank all the people who helped me get my car running.  I couldn't have done it without your help!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||curtis||08-11-2001||11:56 PM||||I just checked the fuel pressure and its good at about 47psi. Isn't the ses light always on before you start? Do you mean when the key is in the run position and your fuel pump is priming?||||reg||5
Z||000008||starfighter007@msn.com||08-12-2001||11:46 AM||||Do you have SPARK??<p>[This message has been edited by starfighter007@msn.com (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||curtis||08-12-2001||11:50 PM||||I checked for spark off the #5 plug and it was there. Someone told me that the cam sprcket could have broke a tooth and still turn over, has anyone seen this?||||reg||1
